@group(:core)
mod Std.Comparable
  ## `Std.Char` supplies `code_point` (Char -> Int) for the `Char` instance's
  ## code-point ordering; `Std.String` makes `String` the transparent
  ## `List(Char)` synonym the lexicographic `String` comparison folds over.
  use Std.Char
  use Std.String
  ## Total-ordering interface: three-way `compare`, returning an `Ordering`.
  ##
  ## `compare/2` is the single method; the comparison *operators* `<`, `>`,
  ## `<=`, `>=` are the surface — on a non-primitive operand they route through
  ## `compare` automatically (`a < b` desugars to `compare(a, b) == LessThan`),
  ## so there are no `lt`/`le`/`gt`/`ge` named helpers to call.
  ##
  ## ## Examples
  ##
  ## ```cure
  ## use Std.Comparable
  ##
  ## compare(1, 2)                           # => LessThan
  ## 'a' < 'b'                               # => true
  ## "ada" < "grace"                         # => true
  ## ```

  ## Group tag consumed by `Cure.Stdlib.Preload`.
  ## Three-way ordering result.
  type Ordering = LessThan | EqualTo | GreaterThan

  ## Total ordering over `T`.
  interface Comparable(t)
    ## `LessThan` when `a < b`, `GreaterThan` when `a > b`, `EqualTo` otherwise.
    fn compare(a: t, b: t) -> Ordering

  ## `Comparable` impl for `Int`.
  implementation Comparable for Int
    ## Integer three-way compare.
    fn compare(a: Int, b: Int) -> Ordering =
      pickup
        a < b -> LessThan
        a > b -> GreaterThan
        else  -> EqualTo

  ## `Comparable` impl for `Float`.
  implementation Comparable for Float
    ## Float three-way compare (NaNs follow BEAM's term-order).
    fn compare(a: Float, b: Float) -> Ordering =
      pickup
        a < b -> LessThan
        a > b -> GreaterThan
        else  -> EqualTo

  ## `Comparable` impl for `Char`: compare Unicode code points. `code_point` is
  ## the `Char -> Int` coercion (Char erases to its code point), so this is an
  ## `Int` comparison — no method dispatch, works on both pipelines.
  implementation Comparable for Char
    ## Character three-way compare on code points.
    fn compare(a: Char, b: Char) -> Ordering =
      pickup
        code_point(a) < code_point(b) -> LessThan
        code_point(a) > code_point(b) -> GreaterThan
        else                          -> EqualTo

  ## Lexicographic three-way compare over `String = List(Char)`: compare heads
  ## by code point, and on a tie recurse into the tails. A prefix sorts before
  ## its extension (`"ad" < "ada"`). Written as a plain top-level recursion (not
  ## a self-recursive interface method) so the impl body carries no nested
  ## method dispatch.
  fn compare_string(a: String, b: String) -> Ordering =
    match a
      [] ->
        match b
          []      -> EqualTo
          [_ | _] -> LessThan
      [ha | ta] ->
        match b
          []        -> GreaterThan
          [hb | tb] ->
            pickup
              code_point(ha) < code_point(hb) -> LessThan
              code_point(ha) > code_point(hb) -> GreaterThan
              else                            -> compare_string(ta, tb)

  ## `Comparable` impl for `String`. Delegates to lexicographic `compare_string`.
  implementation Comparable for String
    ## String three-way compare, character by character.
    fn compare(a: String, b: String) -> Ordering = compare_string(a, b)
